+    "replace": "<p data-narration-id=\"n10\">One of Turnly&rsquo;s most striking dramatic methods is the use of language as a marker of identity and coercion. The play uses English alongside phonetic Japanese and Korean. In several scenes, dialogue begins in Japanese or Korean before returning to English so the audience can follow it. This <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"Moving between two languages or registers within a scene or even a single exchange, used here to signal identity, power, and the pressure to conform.\">code-switching</dfn> can make identity and power audible: Hanako teaches Japanese to Jung Sun while living under coercion in North Korea.</p>",
